lens: one text, three ways to see it, in ed

A lens is a way to see the thing at cur (`design/studio:/a lens shows a
thing/`). ed holds the text, so ed's view shows it three ways, and Tab
turns from one to the next:

	source     the text as written, the only lens typed in
	outline    its items by their indent, as rows, or as thumbs with t,
	           as fm lays out a folder
	render     what the source makes for a person to see: for a note its
	           picture, its parts and the messages between them, as
	           sys/picture lays them out

render is what the text becomes for the eye, whatever form that takes: a
note's picture now, and a scene's animation or a video in time, each by
a renderer for its kind, as the view asks a primitive by its kind
(`design/view:/asked by kind/`). The lens stays one; renderers join it.

The case, carried through: design/arch open in ed
	the bar     source  outline  render, at the top of ed in every lens,
	            over a rule as fm's head is, the one shown lit: a press
	            on a name turns to it
	Tab         the outline: a row an item, two columns in a level, the
	            item the cursor is in lit
	j, enter    the next item, then source on its line
	Tab Tab     the render, the note's picture: the pieces as boxes and the
	            messages between them; Tab once more, or a press on
	            source, is back

Why it is ed's
  A lens is a way ed shows what it holds, so ed says which shows, and
  draws it: the text for source, and for the others a tree of its items,
  which a view lays out as it lays out fm's folder. Every view of ed draws
  what ed sends, the terminal's and gio's window alike, so each shows the
  same lens with nothing of its own to keep. It reads the lines as they
  are, unsaved ones too: the outline is of what is being typed, not of
  the file as it was saved. No state file, no second program, and no
  frame needed: ed in any pane or window has all three.

On the wire
  ed names its lenses on the tags of the tree it draws, and says the one
  shown, but source, in its state. A view draws the names as a bar over
  the text (`view/bar.go:/func Bar/`), and a press on one comes back as a
  key, LENS, whose text is the lens's name (`tty/term.go:/KLens/`).

Read, never typed
  In outline and render no key types, so none changes the text out of
  sight. A move, or a click on an item, puts ed's cursor on its line, so
  source opens where the outline was; enter, esc, a right click or a
  double tap goes to source there; ctrl-s saves, as in every mode
  (`ed/7-loop/16-lenskey.go:/lensKey/`).

What is where
	ed                    the lens shown, the trees it draws, and the
	                      keys in a lens (`ed/7-loop/14-lenses.go`)
	sys/view              outline and render, drawn as it draws fm, and
	                      the bar over them
	ed's terminal view,   draw what ed sends, the bar in place of the
	gio's window          view's head
	outline.Text          the items, by their indent
	sys/picture           a note's render, its picture

What it costs
  - the bar and its rule are two lines of every ed, in any pane: the
    bar alone under twelve lines high, as fm's head is there, and
    neither under three
  - Tab in normal turns the lens; in insert it types a tab, as before

Given up
  - studio show, a lens of its own beside ed: what it showed of the text
    is ed's now; its diff is git diff in the shell, and its run lens
    waited on tests that write what they found
    (`design/studio:/Not built/`)
